<section class="section" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
  <h2 id="pricing-title">Pricing</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Free Cloud images carry a watermark. Pro is a draft bundle: included renders, then a meter.
  </p>
  <div class="price-grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Free</h3>
      <p class="price-figure">Free</p>
      <p>Cloud renders include a small chartkit.dev mark. The open-source library does not draw it.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Watermark on Cloud images</li>
        <li>No key required for a marked image</li>
        <li>Same spec as Pro</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="price-draft">Draft</p>
      <h3>Pro</h3>
      <p class="price-figure">$29<span class="price-unit">/mo</span></p>
      <p>The mark comes off. A bundle of renders is included, and use past that is metered.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Watermark off</li>
        <li>10,000 renders included</li>
        <li>$0.002 each after that</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    $29/mo, 10,000 renders, and $0.002 are draft figures, not a published price. The live Cloud offer is still a
    key that removes the mark. 120 renders a minute per IP is a rate limit, not a quota you can buy.
  </p>
</section>
